* leaking trading-relevant information 
	* this is the least known mode of corruption; but a most important one; because it is very easy to do it without getting caught; to prove that it happened is usually impossible [if the actors do not leak somehow]; just think about how the official statements, even vague ones can move markets considerably
		* for example:
			* someone close to the decision knows that banks will get an extra tax; it informs its crony about the date of the official announcement; the crony has only to short-sell bank stocks around the day of the announcement; even if someone notices it, to prove that the short-selling happened based on side-channel information leak is probably impossible
