			* fake advertisements in crony media
			* ...
* competitive advantage for the crony
	* by legislation with general extent
		* the ruler changes the ruling in favor of the crony or in unfavor of others
			* in controlling: the taxation is especially great tool for the ruler; it is enough to select a few business traits in which the crony differs from its competitors and create tax advantage for those traits
				* examples
					* if the crony has a young bank then the ruler introduces a new extra tax on banks, based on some firm performance in the past [when the cronies bank did not even exist]
					* if the crony has small grocery stores then the ruler raises the food quality examination fee for big groceries or prohibits operating big groceries in sunday or ...
		* obstruction of entrance of new competitors into the market
			* with burdens
				* unnecessary administrational, 'consumer-protective', 'employee-protectee' constrains, which are usually more difficult for smaller firms
			* mandatory licensing for operation and the licenses are decided individually or even limited in number ["concession"]
